ate","anchor":"Check-the-Provisioning-State","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Before showing the ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add to Apple Wallet"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" button, check the current provisioning state for the payment instrument.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let state = await provisioningSession.provisioningState(for: paymentInstrumentId)","","switch state {","case .canProvision(let devices):","    \/\/ Show the \"Add to Apple Wallet\" button.","    \/\/ devices indicates which of phone \/ watch can be provisioned.","case .provisioned(let devices):","    \/\/ Already provisioned on all available devices. Hide or disable the button.","case .cannotProvision(let reason):","    \/\/ Cannot provision. Log reason for diagnostics, and map it to your own","    \/\/ copy for anything the cardholder sees.","}"]},{"text":"Provision the Card","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Provision-the-Card"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"When the cardholder taps ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add to Apple Wallet"}]},{"type":"text","text":", present the native Wallet sheet:"}]},{"code":["guard let viewController = view.window?.rootViewController else { return }","","do {","    let activationState = try await provisioningSession.provision(","        paymentInstrumentId: paymentInstrumentId,","        viewController: viewController","    )","    \/\/ Update your UI based on activationState","} catch CardProvisioningSessionError.provisioningCancelled {","    \/\/ The cardholder or the system dismissed the Apple Pay sheet.","    \/\/ This is not a failure, so leave your UI unchanged.","} catch {","    \/\/ Handle provisioning error","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Handle the Result","anchor":"Handle-the-Result"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"provision(paymentInstrumentId:viewController:)"},{"type":"text","text":" returns a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CardActivationState"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["switch activationState {","case .activated:","    \/\/ Card successfully added and active.","case .requiresActivation:","    \/\/ Card added but requires further activation steps.","case .activating:","    \/\/ Card is currently activating.","case .suspended:","    \/\/ Card suspended by the issuer.","case .deactivated:","    \/\/ Card deactivated.","case .unknown:","    \/\/ State could not be determined.","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Error Handling","anchor":"Error-Handling"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"All session operations throw "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CardProvisioningSessionError"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"level":3,"text":"Match a single case","anchor":"Match-a-single-case","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The error type supports pattern matching, so you can catch one case directly without casting."},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"Matching compares the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"code"},{"text":" only, so it succeeds regardless of the error’s message or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"underlying cause:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["do {","    try await provisioningSession.configure()","} catch CardProvisioningSessionError.couldNotEstablishSession {","    \/\/ Check connectivity and the session token, then retry.","} catch {","    \/\/ Handle everything else.","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"anchor":"Handle-cancellation-gracefully","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Handle cancellation gracefully"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"provisioningCancelled"},{"text":" reports that the Apple Pay sheet was dismissed by the cardholder or by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"the system. Nothing was provisioned and nothing failed, so treat it as a normal outcome. Do not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"present it as an error:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["do {","    _ = try await provisioningSession.provision(","        paymentInstrumentId: paymentInstrumentId,","        viewController: viewController","    )","} catch CardProvisioningSessionError.provisioningCancelled {","    \/\/ Expected when the cardholder taps Cancel. Leave the UI as it was.","} catch {","    \/\/ Log the error for diagnostics, and show your own copy to the cardholder.","    print(error)","    showAlert(yourMessage(for: error))","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"anchor":"Branch-across-several-cases","level":3,"text":"Branch across several cases","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"To handle several failures at once, switch over ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"code"},{"text":". ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Code"},{"type":"text","text":" is non-exhaustive, so always"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"include a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"default"},{"type":"text","text":" case to stay forward compatible with future SDK versions:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["do {","    try await provisioningSession.configure()","} catch let error as CardProvisioningSessionError {","    switch error.code {","    case .noPaymentInstrumentsProvided:","        \/\/ `paymentInstrumentIds` in the configuration was empty.","        break","    case .noKeychainGroupIdProvided:","        \/\/ `keychainAccessGroup` was empty.","        break","    case .couldNotEstablishSession:","        \/\/ Network or authentication failure.","        break","    case .activationDataUnavailable:","        \/\/ Activation data could not be fetched or cached.","        break","    case .provisioningAlreadyInProgress:","        \/\/ A provisioning flow is already running for this payment instrument.","        break","    case .provisioningCancelled:","        \/\/ Dismissed by the cardholder or the system. Not a failure.","        break","    case .provisioningFailed:","        \/\/ PassKit or the provisioning infrastructure reported a failure.","        break","    default:","        break","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"anchor":"Logging","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Logging"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"CardProvisioningSessionError","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CustomStringConvertible"},{"type":"text","text":", so log the error itself:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["print(error)","\/\/ CardProvisioningSessionError.couldNotEstablishSession: deviceRegistration, serverHTTPError. Trace: 00-abc..."],"syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Where the failure came from a network call, "},{"code":"description","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" includes the trace identifier Adyen"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"support needs to correlate the request. Where it came from PassKit, it includes that error’s","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"domain and code. It never contains card data or session tokens, so it is safe to log.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Avoid logging ","type":"text"},{"code":"localizedDescription","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". It carries no diagnostic detail, so the trace identifier is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"lost."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"localizedDescription","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is deliberately short because errors are commonly passed straight to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"UI, but it is not meant for display either: the text is English and is not localized. Map "},{"code":"code","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"to your own copy for anything the cardholder sees."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","text":"Wallet Extension","level":2,"anchor":"Wallet-Extension"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"In addition to in-app provisioning, you can let cardholders provision cards directly from the Apple Wallet app. When configured, your app appears in Wallet’s ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"From Apps on Your iPhone"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" section."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The Sessions approach provides a high-level base class, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"WalletExtensionHandler"},{"type":"text","text":", that handles the full extension flow. You subclass it and override a small set of methods."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Prerequisites","anchor":"Prerequisites"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In-app provisioning must be working first."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"com.apple.developer.payment-pass-provisioning"},{"type":"text","text":" entitlement must be present on the main app, Non-UI Extension, and UI Extension targets."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A shared keychain access group must be configured (the same ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"keychainAccessGroup"},{"type":"text","text":" you passed to "},{"code":"Configuration","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"orderedList"},{"type":"heading","text":"Step 1: Create the Non-UI Extension Target","level":3,"anchor":"Step-1-Create-the-Non-UI-Extension-Target"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"In Xcode, go to ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"File > New > Target","type":"text"}]},{"text":" and select ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent"